lib/build-fex.sh and lib/install-fex-tool.sh are unmodified copies of fex-eac/ from steamac
(FX Steam Launcher, https://github.com/StonkGuy/steamac), Copyright 2026 FX GAMES FZ LLC, Apache-2.0.

frame-vrc downloads or builds FEX from https://github.com/StonkGuy/FEX (MIT, as FEX-Emu). The tool itself ships no FEX binaries,
no game files and no Easy Anti-Cheat files: EAC comes from Valve's Proton EasyAntiCheat Runtime, installed by Steam.
Prebuilt FEX packages (fex-*-steamframe-aarch64.tar.gz, made by `frame-vrc pack`) contain FEX binaries built from that
source, with FEX's MIT license as LICENSE.FEX.
src/frame-vrc-panel (the VR panel) is MIT-licensed (src/frame-vrc-panel/LICENSE), adapted from FrameClash's panel;
its src/third_party_frameeyeosc/ is copied unmodified from frameeyeosc (https://github.com/sasaken1102r/frameeyeosc,
MIT, LICENSE.frameeyeosc next to it), and third_party/openvr/openvr.h is the OpenVR SDK header (BSD-3-Clause, LICENSE
next to it). The panel links SteamVR's own libopenvr_api.so at run time; frame-vrc does not ship it.
